  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1120 AM CDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nThe upper low will weaken and get swept away by the weekend. We\nwill then be within a bridge zone between a strong Bermuda high \nand a strong, hot western ridge. This will keep our temperatures \nseasonably warm - maybe a degree or 2 above normal. This pattern \nwill also keep conditions humid with pop-up showers and storms \neach afternoon. For the most part, chances/coverage will continue\nto be highest (30 to 60 percent) for the Plateau and generally \nlow (20 to 30 percent) for areas west of the Plateau. No severe \nstorms are expected, but gusty winds and heavy downpours will \noccur with some storms. Heat risk levels will be in the 2-3 range \n(out of 4) with peak heat index values pushing mostly into the \n100-105 range.",
